    "The 0.885 GroupKFold-by-patient AUC was computed on the full 160-feature vector, including 119 engineered features derived from multi-day per-patient history (lag1 / roll3 / delta7 / dow / dom). The caregiver screening form only collects the 41 raw daily features — the remaining 119 are filled with the -1 missing sentinel at inference time. Treat the live API number as 'approximate ordering' rather than reproducing the headline AUC; the model is most informative when used as a relative-risk indicator over time, not a single-shot threshold.",
    "Class prevalence in the source TIHM 1.5 cohort is 4.2 % (114 positives of 2 722 rows). cv_precision / cv_recall / cv_f1 at the default 0.5 threshold are intentionally low — the model is cautious about a rare positive class. AUC and average-precision are the meaningful single-shot quality numbers.",
